PROGRAM IMPLEMENTATION 
Drawing System
The drawing tool uses mouse movements to draw lines on the canvas. Each complete drawing action is saved so it can be undone later.
Color Selection
Users can choose their own colors using the color picker or select from six preset colors. The selected color is used for the next drawing action.
Brush Size
The brush size can be adjusted using a slider from 1 to 100. The selected size affects the thickness of lines and shapes.
Eraser Tool
The eraser works by drawing white over the existing content, allowing users to remove unwanted parts of their drawings.
Shape Tools
The application includes line, rectangle, oval, and triangle tools. Users can create shapes by dragging the mouse, and some shapes can be filled with color.
Undo Function
The undo feature allows users to reverse their previous actions, such as drawing, creating shapes, or clearing the canvas.
Clear Canvas
The Clear button displays a confirmation message before removing everything from the canvas. Users can choose Yes or No.
Open and Save Image
Users can open existing PNG, JPG, JPEG, and BMP images and save their finished drawings in supported formats.
Pillow Integration
Pillow handles the image creation and drawing operations, while Tkinter displays the canvas. It also helps keep the displayed drawing and saved image synchronized.

FUNCTIONS USED

clamp_point: Keeps mouse coordinates inside the canvas boundaries.
paint_color: Returns white for the eraser and the chosen color for all other tools.
push_history: Saves the current image before an action so Undo can restore it.
refresh_canvas: Converts the Pillow image with ImageTk and displays it on the Canvas.
update_status: Updates the status bar with the current tool, color, size, and fill state.
make_button: Creates consistently styled buttons for the toolbar.
choose_color: Opens the system color picker.
set_color: Changes the active color and updates the color indicator.
set_tool: Selects a tool and highlights its button.
change_brush_size: Updates brush thickness from the 1 to 100 slider.
toggle_fill: Turns filled shapes on or off.
start_drawing: Begins a stroke or shape and records history.
draw_motion: Draws freehand lines or shows the shape preview.
finish_drawing: Ends a stroke or commits the final shape.
triangle_points: Calculates the three corners of the triangle.
preview_shape_drawing: Draws the temporary shape while dragging.
draw_final_shape: Draws the permanent shape into the Pillow image.
undo: Restores the previous image state.
clear_canvas: Asks for confirmation and then blanks the canvas.
open_image: Loads and fits an external image onto the canvas.
save_image: Saves the Pillow image to a file.
section: Creates a labeled toolbar section.

